// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_SL3_NT_Hetzfeld_L_Task3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AntiMutagenClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3798433333" "Anti-Mutagen Injector"
// DetailString :
"P792468284" "This compact device is loaded with a finite number of doses that has a range of approximately twenty yards. A single dose is, according to Dr. Hetzfeld, enough to combat the genetic abnormalities in the majority of Neuron's failed experiments, particularly the ghouls."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CureAdministeredClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1307630080" "Cure Administered"
// DetailString :
"P4125498769" "You completed your task in administering the anti-mutagen cure to a number of ghouls in the tunnels. Dr. Hetzfeld will be eager to receive your first hand report of the field test of his anti-mutagen injector."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MoreContagiousClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1335910467" "It's Spreading!"
// DetailString :
"P620068948" "Just in the short amount of time you've been down here you have seen the mutation spread geometrically. This isn't a problem, it's the making of an epidemic!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ProblemClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4193045211" "We've Got a Problem"
// DetailString :
"P607262906" "According to Dr. Hetzfeld there is a problem with the anti-mutagen. Apparently his test subject in the lab, which had initially shown great strides in recovering from genetic deformation, had reverted, and the mutation amplified. This was bad enough, but in addition to worsening the test subject's condition, it also apparently became resistant to the anti-mutagen as well as transmissible and has infected the control subjects, mutating them into carriers in a matter of minutes.<br><br>This means that the experiments you administered the treatment to down in the tunnels, have probably begun reverting, mutating, and spreading the mutation to others."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ProblemSolvedClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4144360686" "Epidemic Avoided"
// DetailString :
"P3343755722" "Thanks to your quick actions the mutation had only spread through a small section of the tunnels. Had even one of those mutants gotten into a pocket of Ghouls who knows how much damage could have been done."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2318905469" "Neuron prides himself on his speed, but he seldom worries about the cost of his erratic experimentations. That care free attitude will now cost him. If successful, I will show Emperor Cole the true brilliance of Dr. Hetzfeld, and Neuron's foolishness will be put to rest once and for all. Aid me in this endeavor and your rewards will be immense!"
// SendOffString :
"P1914492210" "I knew you would see the logic of my offer. Neuron's myriad failed genetic experiments are not as flawed as he initially believed. I have concocted an anti-mutagen that should counteract their negative effects, while keeping the benefits of Neuron's sloppy genetic tinkering. I want you to test the mutagen in the field on the ghouls down in the tunnels beneath Neutropolis."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_SL3_NT_Hetzfeld_L_Task3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P858941087" "Administer cure to Failed Experiments"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2970219287" "You'll find the highest concentration of failed experiments in the tunnels beneath Neutropolis. Once you have administered the anti-mutagen report back to me."
// tokenprogressstring :
"P452021072" "You have cured {token} of 20"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2560813949" "Here is the anti-mutagen injector. It's range is relatively short, but a single dose should be enough to cure the genetic abnormalities of the target."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3692180098" "You've done that thing a lot."

